5. Free redistribution and modifications

Anyone may redistribute unmodified or modified Covered Material, in source or
binary form, without charge, for recipients to exercise the permissions in
this license. This includes public source forks and free download mirrors,
but not hosted access to the learning application, paid bundles, or provision
as part of a professional or organizational learning service.

You must include this entire LICENSE, preserve copyright, attribution and
third-party notices, identify your modifications prominently, and supply the
corresponding source for any Covered Material you distribute in binary form,
including your modifications, without an additional fee. You must license your
modifications to Covered Material to recipients under Part A of this license.
Do not impose additional restrictions on recipients' permissions under this
license. Recipients receive their permission for the licensor's Covered
Material directly from the licensor; you cannot grant broader rights to it.
These conditions apply only to Covered Material and adaptations of it, not to
separate works, excluded MIT material or third-party components.

6. Contributions

Contributors retain ownership of their contributions. Sharing a fork or opening
